  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>b</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>, be two vectors. If <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>, is a vector such that <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math> and <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#8901;</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi></math> then <math><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#8901;</mo><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover></math>, is equal to."
